note: function-level scope + bridging a global variable with `global`

set number counter to 0

func increment() do:
    global counter
    change counter to counter + 1
end

increment()
increment()
increment()
print(f"counter = {counter}")

note: constants must be uppercase; a later change is a runtime error
set constant number MAX_RETRIES to 3
print(f"MAX_RETRIES = {MAX_RETRIES}")
